o sessions as JSON pointers, with `patch`: the ops that turn `before` into `after` when `patchable`.", "inputSchema": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"after": {"description": "Session id to diff to", "type": "string"}, "before": {"description": "Session id to diff from", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["after", "before"], "type": "object"}, "name": "diff"}, {"annotations": {"readOnlyHint": false}, "description": "Apply patch ops atomically and return the new revision. `set` replaces the value at a JSON pointer in a node record (`{\"op\":\"set\",\"node\":\"box\",\"path\":\"/opacity\",\"value\":0.5}`), `set_document` one in the document, `remove` drops a subtree.", "inputSchema": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"base_revision": {"description": "Revision the ops were written against; a stale revision fails with `conflict`. Defaults to the current revision.", "format": "uint64", "minimum": 0.0, "type": ["integer", "null"]}, "ops": {"description": "Ops applied in order; any failure rejects them all", "items": {"description": "One edit of the document.", "oneOf": [{"description": "Replace the value at JSON pointer `path` inside the node record, such as `/opacity` or `/body/text`. Identity and tree fields (`/id`, `/parent`, `/children`) are fixed.", "properties": {"node": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"description": "Stable identity. Matches `director-core`'s generational `NodeId`.", "properties": {"generation": {"description": "Slot generation. A recycled slot has a new generation.", "format": "uint32", "minimum": 0.0, "type": "integer"}, "index": {"description": "Arena slot.", "format": "uint32", "minimum": 0.0, "type": "integer"}}, "required": ["generation", "index"], "type": "object"}], "description": "A node by authored name (an HTML `id`) or by generational id."}, "op": {"enum": ["set"], "type": "string"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "value": true}, "required": ["node", "op", "path", "value"], "type": "object"}, {"description": "Replace the value at JSON pointer `path` of the document, such as `/fps` or `/timeline/tracks/0/clips/0/duration`. `/version` is fixed and `/nodes` changes through the node ops.", "properties": {"op": {"enum": ["set_document"], "type": "string"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "value": true}, "required": ["op", "path", "value"], "type": "object"}, {"description": "Remove the node and its subtree. A clip's scene root or a mask that a remaining node uses cannot be removed.", "properties": {"node": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"description": "Stable identity. Matches `director-core`'s generational `NodeId`.", "properties": {"generation": {"description": "Slot generation. A recycled slot has a new generation.", "format": "uint32", "minimum": 0.0, "type": "integer"}, "index": {"description": "Arena slot.", "format": "uint32", "minimum": 0.0, "type": "integer"}}, "required": ["generation", "index"], "type": "object"}], "description": "A node by authored name (an HTML `id`) or by generational id."}, "op": {"enum": ["remove"], "type": "string"}}, "required": ["node", "op"], "type": "object"}]}, "type": "array"}, "session": {"description": "Session id from `open`", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["ops", "session"], "type": "object"}, "name": "patch"}, {"annotations": {"readOnlyHint": true}, "description": "Source ids, layout bounds, timeline and audio of the current revision at a time.", "inputSchema": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"session": {"description": "Session id from `open`", "type": "string"}, "time": {"default": 0.0, "description": "Seconds into the timeline", "format": "double", "type": "number"}}, "required": ["session"], "type": "object"}, "name": "inspect"}, {"annotations": {"readOnlyHint": true}, "description": "Score the current revision 0-100 for publishing. Errors cost 20: missing fonts, nodes never on the canvas, clipped or non-finite audio. Warnings cost 5: text clipped by the canvas edge or inside the safe-zone inset for a second or more, captions over faces, reframed subjects out of frame, true peak above -1 dBTP, a silent mix, loudness more than 2 LU off target. Static stretches are info. `pass` holds with no errors. Each issue carries the authored node name, time range and a fix.", "inputSchema": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"every": {"default": 0.25, "description": "Seconds between layout samples", "format": "double", "type": "number"}, "loudness_target": {"default": -14.0, "description": "Integrated loudness target of the audio mix in LUFS", "format": "double", "type": "number"}, "safe_zone": {"description": "Safe-zone preset for text: `tiktok`, `youtube_shorts`, `instagram_reel`, `instagram_story`, `linkedin`, `twitter`, `mobile` or `desktop`", "type": ["string", "null"]}, "session": {"description": "Session id from `open`", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["session"], "type": "object"}, "name": "qa"}, {"annotations": {"readOnlyHint": false}, "description": "Paint one frame of the current revision as PNG.", "inputSchema": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"output": {"description": "Write the PNG here and return its path; without it the PNG returns as image content", "type": ["string", "null"]}, "session": {"description": "Session id from `open`", "type": "string"}, "time": {"default": 0.0, "description": "Seconds into the timeline", "format": "double", "type": "number"}}, "required": ["session"], "type": "object"}, "name": "render_frame"}, {"annotations": {"readOnlyHint": false}, "description": "Export the current revision as a video file. Fails with `missing_font` when required fonts are absent.", "inputSchema": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"alpha": {"description": "Leave uncovered pixels clear and write VP9 with alpha", "type": ["boolean", "null"]}, "draft": {"default": false, "description": "Software x264 ultrafast at CRF 30", "type": "boolean"}, "encoder": {"default": "software", "description": "Video encoder", "enum": ["software", "nvenc"], "t